% change — the lane change, a unit of the road family a CAR'S planner includes and a chair's does not (road-family
% s-f62c0ed8, spec/18 §2.3 and §3: a leavable block lives in a unit of its own; derivation by unit choice, never by
% override). It brings the family's planner (planner_domain.llp) with it, so a program includes THIS unit for the planner
% with the lane change, or planner_domain.llp alone for the planner without it. The keep-table's mleft/mright: a lane
% change only to an adjacent lane (the host says adjacent(D) only of one), its lead and follower safe, the ego not just arrived from that side, no conflict zone
% near (roomy: the facts are the planner's). The rule's block comes BEFORE the include, so it stays the progress stage's
% first rule as in the one-file planner (a second stage block of one stage merges with the first, in order): the car's
% planner bundle is byte-identical to the one-file planner's, and so is the road's image.
catalog change 1.
provenance text "the road family's lane change, the car's unit (from planner_domain.llp, road-world s-e812715d step 2)" "2026-11-01".
% The lanes' kinds (road-scenarios s-e23be780, record 20261105T082838-463d7d, 2026-11-05): a town's net carries parking and
% bidirectional centre lanes beside its driving ones (Town03; CARLA counts the ego on a bidirectional lane outside the
% route). The host says each lane's KIND (vocabulary, rule 2: geometry in the host, classes in the rules): own_kind(K) of the
% ego's lane, lane_kind(D, K) of each side every tick (none: no same-direction lane there). The reasons are the rules':
%   change        a person's wish (change_reason(D), road_wishes.py: a wish is the only change_reason the host states)
%   change_pass   a slow lead: pass it on a DRIVING side
%   change_aside  a slow lead and no driving side: pass it on the centre or parking lane (the pass itself, never a stay)
%   change_back   on a lane off the route's (parking, bidirectional): back to a driving lane beside
% side_clear(D) (surprise-kinds s-7a02c2ac, spec 20 §2, the architect's (B)): the host's verdict that the {D} side is free to
% change into: adjacent(D) and each of its two roles (its lead, its follower) unfilled or safe by the fold (safe_long and
% safe_lat), stated only for an adjacent same-direction side. An unfilled role gets role_empty(R) and no safety fact (no
% filler). No rule reads side_lead / side_follow or a role's safe_* now; they stay as vocabulary, stated for FILLED roles,
% for a pack that names the side's L or F (a closing follower, a lead's signal), never to fake an empty role.
% A wish and a pass naming opposite sides in one tick are two enabled rules of equal prior: the sampler's draw decides
% (as when change_reason named both sides before), not the rules' order; the case wish_against_pass records the seeded draw:
% the wish (change) fires.
stage progress {
  %% A person wishes me on the {D} lane, it is safe ahead and behind, and I did not just leave it: I change to it.
  change [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $change_reason(D) * $settled(D) * $side_clear(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * $roomy(C) * go -o ().
  %% A slow lead ahead and a driving lane on my {D} side, safe ahead and behind, and I did not just leave it: I pass on it.
  change_pass [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $lead_slow * $adjacent(D) * $lane_kind(D, driving) * $settled(D) * $side_clear(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * $roomy(C) * go -o ().
  %% A slow lead ahead and no driving lane on my {E} side: I pass on the {D} lane, a {K} one, safe ahead and behind.
  change_aside [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $lead_slow * $adjacent(D) * $lane_kind(D, K) * off_route(K) * other_side(D, E) * $lane_kind(E, X) * not_driving(X) * $settled(D) * $side_clear(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * $roomy(C) * go -o ().
  %% I drive on a {K} lane, off the route's, and the {D} lane beside is a driving one, safe ahead and behind: I change back to it.
  change_back [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $own_kind(K) * off_route(K) * $adjacent(D) * $lane_kind(D, driving) * $settled(D) * $side_clear(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * $roomy(C) * go -o ().
  %% A car stands in my lane, no lane of mine on my {E} side, and the oncoming {D} lane is clear for the whole pass: I pass through it.
  change_oncoming [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $lead_standing * $oncoming(D) * $oncoming_clear(D) * other_side(D, E) * $lane_kind(E, X) * not_driving(X) * $settled(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * $roomy(C) * go -o ().
  %% My lane leaves my route ahead and the {D} lane carries it on, free: I change to it.
  change_route [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $route_lane(D) * $adjacent(D) * $lane_kind(D, driving) * $settled(D) * $side_clear(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * not_in(C) * go -o ().
}
include "planner_domain.llp".
% The gap records (road-scenarios s-e23be780 step 3, steps/road-gap-vocabulary-architect.md; the vocabulary is the architect's,
% planner_domain.llp, stated by the host in the EGO's heading frame):
%   change_route           20261105T151048-ec8088 (commonroad-world s-9b7591fb step 2): the ego's lane does not continue along
%                          its route (CommonRoad's USA_Peach-4_5_T-1: the straight way on leaves from the two right lanes only);
%                          route_lane(D) is the host's, the change allowed up to the junction's line (not_in), not only where roomy
%   change_oncoming        20261105T051440-668e45: a car standing in the only lane, the oncoming lane lent for the whole pass
%                          (oncoming_clear: the host's verdict, the lead and follower of that lane included; busy or unseen:
%                          nothing fires, the ego waits behind it); back home by change_back (own_kind(oncoming), off route)
%   change_emergency_right 20261105T051440-13b2f9: an emergency vehicle behind me: I move over, to the right first (keep right);
%   change_emergency_left  to the left when no driving lane is on my right, or (change_emergency_left_busy) when the right one is
%                          busy (side_busy: the host's complement of side_clear, the architect's ruling). A yield, so a SAFETY block: it comes before any
%                          progress (it takes `now`, the beat's plan is the move). The side is bound through other_side, so the
%                          command carries D. No lane free: no rule, the ego holds its lane.
stage safety {
  %% An emergency vehicle comes up behind me and the {D} lane on my right is a driving one, free: I move over for it.
  change_emergency_right [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $emergency(follower) * other_side(D, left) * $adjacent(D) * $lane_kind(D, driving) * $settled(D) * $side_clear(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * $roomy(C) * now -o ().
  %% An emergency vehicle comes up behind me, no driving lane on my right, and the {D} lane on my left is a driving one, free: I move over for it.
  change_emergency_left [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $emergency(follower) * other_side(D, right) * $lane_kind(right, X) * not_driving(X) * $adjacent(D) * $lane_kind(D, driving) * $settled(D) * $side_clear(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * $roomy(C) * now -o ().
  %% An emergency vehicle comes up behind me, the lane on my right is busy, and the {D} lane on my left is a driving one, free: I move over for it.
  change_emergency_left_busy [dyn] : $busy * $tick__grant(planner, controls) * $emergency(follower) * other_side(D, right) * $side_busy(right) * $adjacent(D) * $lane_kind(D, driving) * $settled(D) * $side_clear(D) * $zone_at(nextzone, C) * $roomy(C) * now -o ().
}
% the host's lane kinds (road_facts.py) and their classes
types (lkind).                              % completed by the instance (capacity.llp)
pred own_kind(lkind) : planner.             % the kind of the ego's lane
pred lane_kind(side, lkind) : planner.      % the kind of the lane on that side, every tick (none: no same-direction lane)
pred side_clear(side) : planner.            % that side free to change into: adjacent, its lead and follower each unfilled or safe
pred side_busy(side) : planner.             % its complement: an adjacent side NOT free to change into (stated where side_clear is not; 13b2f9)
bwd off_route(lkind).                       % a lane the route does not run on: a pass may use it, a stay may not
off_route(parking).
off_route(bidirectional).
off_route(oncoming).                        % the opposite direction's lane: lent for a pass (change_oncoming), never a stay (668e45)
pred route_lane(side) : planner.            % my lane leaves my route ahead and the lane on that side carries it on (the host's, from the net's
                                            % connections: stated early enough to change while the zone is far, never inside a junction; ec8088)
bwd not_in(zclass).                         % where a route change is allowed: up to the junction's line, never inside it
not_in(none).
not_in(far).
not_in(near).
not_in(at).
bwd not_driving(lkind).                     % no driving lane there
not_driving(parking).
not_driving(bidirectional).
not_driving(none).
bwd other_side(side, side).
other_side(left, right).
other_side(right, left).
